    "facts": "SPI uses 64-byte chunks and polls with 10 us waits; after 25 unsuccessful polls it requests a one-ms task delay. Display flush shares a single configured deadline (20 ms in this study).",
    "inference": "Scheduling delays during slower chunk transfers may contribute to the observed 1 MHz timeout groups. No per-device timing or transfer-completion instrumentation was collected, so this is not a measured root-cause conclusion."
